Schaeffler is a dynamic global technology company and its success has been a result of its entrepreneurial spirit and long history of private ownership. Does that sound interesting to you? As a partner to all of the major automobile manufacturers, as well as key players in the aerospace and industrial sectors, we offer you many development opportunities.

Your Key Responsibilities

Design, develop, and maintain scalable full-stack applications and SaaS solutions running in cloud environments;
Implement backend services, APIs, and frontend components using suitable frameworks and programming languages;
Maintain, refactor, debug, and improve existing applications and services;
Develop and deliver new features based on business and user requirements;
Ensure high code quality through code reviews, coding guidelines, and test-driven development practices;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define solution architectures and implement robust technical designs;
Contribute to cloud deployment and operational readiness of applications on AWS, and Azure;
Support CI/CD and automation practices using tools such as GitHub Actions, and Terraform;
Take technical responsibility for applications throughout their lifecycle as part of an agile product or engineering team.

Your Qualifications

University degree in (business) informatics or alternative training with relevant professional experience in this field;
At least 5 years of relevant professional experience in software engineering / full-stack development;
Very good experience in developing applications as well as SaaS solutions in full stack running on cloud resources such as AWS, Azure, and/or Google C;
Knowledge in common backend programming languages such as Python, C#, Go, and/or Java, as well as JavaScript / TypeScript for frontend development, is essential;
Knowledge of common API design patterns and TDD (Test-Driven Development) is a must;
Familiarity with software engineering principles and patterns such as DRY, KISS, and microservices;
Experience with code reviews and coding guidelines, including establishing, improving, and following development standards;
Proven experience in maintaining, refactoring, debugging, and improving existing codebases, as well as implementing new features;
Knowledge of common backend frameworks such as FastAPI, .NET Core, Gin, or similar;
Knowledge of frontend frameworks such as Angular, Vue, React, or similar;
Knowledge of CI/CD using GitHub Actions and/or Jenkins, as well as Infrastructure as Code using Terraform, is a very welcome plus;
Fluent in English, spoken and written;
Ability and willingness to coach and to take responsibility for services;
Strong hands-on attitude combined with good analytical skills;
Ability to learn new technologies and skills (T-Shape philosophy);
Proficiency in agile methodologies, with experience working effectively within agile teams and environments, fostering an agile mindset in daily work.

Our Offering

Onboarding & Integration: we help you settle in quickly through our onboarding program and a team that supports you;
Health & Life Insurance: we provide private health plans and life insurance, so you can have peace of mind;
Discounts: enjoy discounts from our partners on activities, trainings, goods etc.;
Bookster Subscription: are you a passionate reader? Then you can borrow your favorite books from the Bookster Library;
Professional Development: with our variety of projects and teams, you'll be able to learn new skills, develop and shape the career path that fits you best;
